cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "matisse"
abstract: >-
  A C++23 library that reads the definition of a real tokenizer, decides where its output can be cut with certainty,
  and encodes text in parallel by cutting only there, with token ids byte-identical to the sequential encoding. The
  first version covers GPT-2, cl100k_base and o200k_base, whose pre-tokenizer patterns have exact verifiers, and reports
  the certified windows of a byte-level merge table without a pre-tokenizer through the lazy certification.
keywords:
  - tokenization
  - byte-pair encoding
  - pre-tokenization
  - parallel encoding
  - C++
authors:
